Child of tracker 0266 (pillage manifest,
docs/pillage-0266-agentic-reproduction-2026-07-12.md, technique 7).

## Context

skill-doctor clusters failures by ad hoc named signatures with no shared
upper vocabulary; verify-gate's REROLL rationale is freeform prose. The
paper's five-way error taxonomy (arXiv:2604.21965 §5.3) gives a reusable
"why did this fail" category. This is a labeling convention (like the
verifiable:/consider:/nofollow: minor tags), not a mechanical detector.

## Actions

1. Reframe for the harness: Agent Error (implementer misread ticket/rule) /
   Extractor Error (ticket underspecified) / Original Error (pre-existing
   bug) / Missing Data (missing context or access) / Other.
2. Add a required root_cause_class field to verify-gate's REROLL rationale
   and to skill-doctor's per-pattern rows.
3. Document the five categories with one example each in both SKILL.md
   files.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] verify-gate REROLL verdicts carry root_cause_class, documented
- [ ] skill-doctor survey output tags each pattern with root_cause_class
- [ ] Both SKILL.md files document the taxonomy
